// contracts/proto/tl/raft/v1/raft.proto: Raft between durable server
// chapter: content/courses/ai-platform-engineering/05-durable-orchestration-and-workers/10-raft-ha.md
// replicas (optional dur.10). Served on :7234 in Kubernetes.
// The messages are those of figure 2 (RequestVote, AppendEntries) and
// figure 13 (InstallSnapshot) of Ongaro and Ousterhout, "In Search of an
// Understandable Consensus Algorithm" (2014). Each log entry carries exactly
// one framed WAL record (formats/wal.md), so Raft replicates the bytes the
// single-node server writes.
//
// Peers are numbered by [durable].raft.id (1-based). A follower answers a
// client rpc of tl.durable.v1 with UNAVAILABLE and the gRPC trailer
// `tl-raft-leader: <host:port>` naming the leader it knows, or no trailer
// during an election.
